A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus tells of a man who plants a vineyard, lets it out and goes away; of servants sent for the fruit and refused, beaten and killed; of a son sent last, cast out and killed; and of the owner’s coming, which is asked about and answered. Jesus quotes the stone the builders rejected, and in Matthew says the kingdom of God shall be taken from those He addresses and given to a nation bringing forth the fruits thereof. Jesus explains none of the parts.'))
